# The stock, pre-mounted nozzle on CORE One / CORE One+ / CORE One L --
# a genuine Bondtech CHT core (Prusa's CORE One L blog says so verbatim).
# HF is the DEFAULT hardware on these machines, not an upgrade.
name = Prusa Nozzle brass CHT 0.4
vendor = prusa
tip = brass
diameter = 0.4
high_flow = 1
abrasive_ok = 0
preset_variant = HF0.4
retract = 0.7
retract_speed = 45
default_layer_h = 0.2
default_width = 0.45
default_speed_external = 200
default_speed_perimeter = 150
default_speed_infill = 150
default_speed_travel = 350
claim_mvs_pla = 21
claim_mvs_petg = 22
claim_mvs_abs = 25
claim_mvs_pc = 22
claim_mvs_pa = 10
note = [sourced] No manufacturer flow table exists for the CHT brass; the
note = claim_mvs values above are Prusa's OWN bundle-2.5.5 HF0.4 filament
note = preset ceilings (*PLAHF* 21 / *PETHF* 22 / ABS 25 / PC 22 / PA 10) --
note = the lowest trust tier in this database. Prusa markets +45% to +114%
note = vs standard brass (MK4S announcement) -- UNVERIFIED and inconsistent
note = with E3D's published HF tables, which top out at +82% (0.6 PLA) and
note = show only +25-50% at this 0.4 diameter. Plan around +25-33% at 0.4.
note = [sourced] CHT geometry: filament split into three streams and heated
note = from the inside (Bondtech patent; help.prusa3d.com). MMU3 use warned
note = against in the Prusa KB.
note = [independent] tomshardware.com CORE One review ran Prusament PETG at
note = 26 mm3/s clean on this nozzle (works-at datapoint, not a ceiling).
note = [independent] makezine MK4S review: PLA drafts sustained 28-30 mm3/s
note = (draft quality, no underextrusion metric).
